Subject: [PATCH] quest POI: the void plane is not ground

The party leader died every five minutes for weeks, always self inflicted,
always in Ashenvale, and five previous fixes went at fall arithmetic because
the core reports the kill as fall damage. It is not a fall. Something teleports
the character to one fixed point below the world, and that point is a quest
POI whose height resolved to the plane the core kills at.

MEASURED, NOT REASONED

44 deaths in six and a half hours, at one coordinate, identical to the last
decimal every time:

    pos            2384.000000, -3422.000000, -502.411011   map 1, zone 331
    killer         self, 44 of 44
    last seen      seven different places, 200 yards apart, all at z 122 to 154

x and y are EXACT INTEGERS. Nothing that walks or falls lands on 2384.000000.
They were written, and `quest_poi_points` holds exactly one row carrying them:

    QuestID 9518  Idx1 0  Idx2 0  X 2384  Y -3422     (Agents of Destruction)

Objective 0's POI is a SINGLE point, so the weighted centroid the lookup builds
over `qPoi.points` is that point unchanged, integers and all. The leader holds
9518 at QUEST_STATUS_INCOMPLETE, which is why this runs through the incomplete
branch and DoIncompleteQuest.

Three of the 44 rows caught the character mid-arrival, one second or less
before it died:

    last seen      2384.000000, -3422.000000, -500.000000

Exactly MIN_HEIGHT. Not near it. The character is PLACED on the void plane,
falls 2.411 yards in the following tick, and the core deals full health as
DAMAGE_FALL_TO_VOID.

WHY THE HEIGHT COMES OUT AT -500

The shipped grid was read back out of the running image and a `getHeight` /
`getLiquidLevel` reader validated against stored positions before any of this
was believed. It reproduces them to three decimals:

    gameobject 181686   stored z 110.442      computed 110.4429
    gameobject 181687   stored z 110.416      computed 110.4173
    sampled character   stored z 109.795998   computed 109.7955

At the POI, on map 1 tile 27/38:

    getHeight(2384, -3422)        = -100000.0   the cell is a TERRAIN HOLE
    getLiquidLevel(2384, -3422)   =    -500.0   the liquid map's filler
    std::max of the two           =    -500.0

Only 28 of that tile's 16384 cells are holes, 0.17%, and the POI's integer
coordinate sits inside one. Eight yards north the ground is at 110.22, which is
where the quest objects actually stand.

The second number is the one that matters. Where there is no liquid the map
carries a filler, and on this tile that filler is -500.0f in 14357 of 16641
cells, 86%. It is numerically MIN_HEIGHT. So `std::max(GetHeight, GetWaterLevel)`
over a hole does not return a sentinel; it returns the void plane, dressed as a
height, on 86% of the tile.

WHY THE EXISTING GUARD DOES NOT CATCH IT

    if (dz == INVALID_HEIGHT || dz == VMAP_INVALID_HEIGHT_VALUE)

-500.0f is neither. It is not -100000.0f and it is not -200000.0f, so the test
passes and dz is treated as ground. `DoIncompleteQuest` writes
`WorldPosition(mapId, 2384, -3422, -500)` into `data.pos`, and `MoveFarTo`
teleports the bot onto it once the walk has failed to close the gap five times:

    return bot->TeleportTo(dest);        NewRpgBaseAction.cpp

That teleport is why the driver column reads idle, errand and unattributed
across the deaths, and why the last sampled position is anywhere within 200
yards. The bot wanders normally for thirty to seventy seconds accumulating
stuck attempts against a destination 600 yards underground, then is moved to it
from wherever it happens to be standing. No drive of the module's is involved
at all.

WHAT THIS CHANGES

`dz <= MIN_HEIGHT` is refused at all four sites that compute this value: both
branches of GetQuestPOIPosAndObjectiveIdx, which offer the candidate, and
DoIncompleteQuest and DoCompletedQuest, which build the destination that gets
teleported to. The two sites patch 0010 already touches take it as an `else`,
so the unloaded-grid forgiveness there is untouched: that branch leaves dz at a
sentinel on purpose, and a sentinel is below MIN_HEIGHT too.

Refusing is safe by construction rather than by judgement. The core kills at
`z < GetMinHeight(x, y)`, and GetMinHeight returns MIN_HEIGHT wherever a tile
carries no flight bounds, which is every tile on maps 0 and 1. A destination at
or below that plane is one the core would kill a character for reaching, so
there is no legitimate destination being lost.

WHAT IS NOT FIXED, DELIBERATELY

The bot no longer dies, and it also no longer walks to objective 0 of quest
9518: that objective's only POI point is refused, so the lookup falls through to
the quest's other incomplete objectives, or to ChangeToIdle when none is left.
Resolving a real height NEAR a holed POI instead of refusing it would be the
better answer and is not attempted here, because it cannot be measured from
outside a running image and this patch is the half that stops the killing.

WHAT WOULD LET THIS PATCH BE DELETED: upstream refusing a destination below
MIN_HEIGHT at either site, or `GetWaterLevel`'s no-liquid filler ceasing to
collide with the void plane constant.

APPLIES TO: mod-playerbots @ 8d9f6aa6bc6d45f9ae0ee0675b9b1f8aa6937312,
NewRpgBaseAction::GetQuestPOIPosAndObjectiveIdx (both branches),
NewRpgDoQuestAction::DoIncompleteQuest and NewRpgDoQuestAction::DoCompletedQuest,
on top of patch 0010.
diff --git a/src/Ai/World/Rpg/Action/NewRpgAction.cpp b/src/Ai/World/Rpg/Action/NewRpgAction.cpp
index 26d49f1a..f2f9c940 100644
--- a/src/Ai/World/Rpg/Action/NewRpgAction.cpp
+++ b/src/Ai/World/Rpg/Action/NewRpgAction.cpp
@@ -570,6 +570,16 @@ bool NewRpgDoQuestAction::DoIncompleteQuest(NewRpgInfo::DoQuest& data)
         if (dz == INVALID_HEIGHT || dz == VMAP_INVALID_HEIGHT_VALUE)
             return false;
 
+        // infra: THE VOID PLANE IS NOT A DESTINATION, AND THIS IS THE SITE
+        // THAT KILLS. The WorldPosition built below is stored in data.pos and
+        // handed to MoveFarTo, which teleports the bot straight onto it once
+        // the walk has failed to close the gap five times. A dz of -500.0f
+        // therefore lands the character under the world, where the core deals
+        // full health as a void kill and reports it as fall damage. Refuse
+        // instead: there is no height here worth walking to.
+        if (dz <= MIN_HEIGHT)
+            return false;
+
         WorldPosition pos(bot->GetMapId(), dx, dy, dz);
         data.lastReachPOI = 0;
         data.pos = pos;
@@ -673,6 +683,11 @@ bool NewRpgDoQuestAction::DoCompletedQuest(NewRpgInfo::DoQuest& data)
                 return false;
             dz = bot->GetPositionZ();
         }
+        // infra: THE VOID PLANE IS NOT A DESTINATION. Same teleport, same
+        // death, on the turn-in half. `else` so the substitution above keeps
+        // its provisional z.
+        else if (dz <= MIN_HEIGHT)
+            return false;
 
         WorldPosition pos(bot->GetMapId(), dx, dy, dz);
         data.lastReachPOI = 0;
diff --git a/src/Ai/World/Rpg/Action/NewRpgBaseAction.cpp b/src/Ai/World/Rpg/Action/NewRpgBaseAction.cpp
index 9f4df925..17edeb72 100644
--- a/src/Ai/World/Rpg/Action/NewRpgBaseAction.cpp
+++ b/src/Ai/World/Rpg/Action/NewRpgBaseAction.cpp
@@ -942,6 +942,13 @@ bool NewRpgBaseAction::GetQuestPOIPosAndObjectiveIdx(uint32 questId, std::vector
                 if (bot->GetMap()->IsGridLoaded(dx, dy))
                     continue;
             }
+            // infra: THE VOID PLANE IS NOT GROUND. Checked as an `else` so the
+            // unloaded-grid forgiveness above is untouched: that branch leaves
+            // dz at a sentinel deliberately, and a sentinel is below
+            // MIN_HEIGHT too. See the incomplete branch below for the full
+            // note.
+            else if (dz <= MIN_HEIGHT)
+                continue;
 
             // THE SAME-ZONE FILTER IS GONE. It is what stranded every bot with
             // an out-of-zone turn-in: the POI was discarded, poiInfo came back
@@ -1024,6 +1031,16 @@ bool NewRpgBaseAction::GetQuestPOIPosAndObjectiveIdx(uint32 questId, std::vector
         if (dz == INVALID_HEIGHT || dz == VMAP_INVALID_HEIGHT_VALUE)
             continue;
 
+        // infra: THE VOID PLANE IS NOT GROUND. `GetWaterLevel` returns the
+        // liquid map's filler where there is no liquid, and on a shipped
+        // tile that filler is -500.0f - numerically MIN_HEIGHT, the plane
+        // the core kills at. So where `GetHeight` fails over a terrain
+        // hole, `std::max` of the two hands back exactly -500.0f, which is
+        // neither sentinel above and passes the test as if it were ground.
+        // Measured: 86% of tile 0012738's liquid cells hold -500.0f.
+        if (dz <= MIN_HEIGHT)
+            continue;
+
         if (bot->GetZoneId() != bot->GetMap()->GetZoneId(bot->GetPhaseMask(), dx, dy, dz))
             continue;
 
